.TH ELECTRIC-EYE 1 "October 2026" "electric-eye 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
electric-eye \- query and inspect the electric-eyed activity monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B electric-eye
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B electric-eye
is the read-only client for
.BR electric-eyed (8).
It queries a Unix socket and can render human-readable output or structured JSON.
It never modifies capture state or configuration.
.PP
The optional
.B tui
command provides an interactive, read-only terminal dashboard.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print pretty JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-jsonl
Print one JSON object per line.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Limit results to 1..1000.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Use an alternate daemon query socket.
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp-socket " PATH"
Use an alternate MCP bridge socket.
.TP
.BI \-\-since " TIME"
Only include results since a relative time (for example
.BR 15m ", " 1h ", " 24h )
or an epoch timestamp.
.TP
.BI \-\-before " TIME"
Only include results before a relative time or epoch timestamp.
.TP
.BI \-\-cursor " CURSOR"
Resume after the opaque
.B next_cursor
value returned by a previous activity or incident query.
.TP
.BI \-\-severity " LEVEL"
For incidents, filter to
.BR low ", " medium ", or " high .
.TP
.BI \-\-rule " TEXT"
For incidents, filter by rule or title substring.
.TP
.BI \-\-app " TEXT"
For incidents, filter by application or executable substring.
.TP
.BI \-\-netns " TEXT"
For flows, netns and explain, filter by namespace, container, unit or context label substring.
.TP
.BI \-\-role " TEXT"
For flows, netns and explain, filter by flow role substring.
.TP
.B \-\-unacked
For incidents, hide locally acknowledged or muted entries.
.TP
.BI \-\-for " DURATION"
Lifetime for
.B ack
or
.B mute
(for example
.BR 30m " or " 1h ).
.TP
.B \-\-follow
For
.BR activity ,
stream new events until interrupted.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tui
Interactive terminal dashboard with Overview, Incidents, Activity, Apps & Flows, and Noise views.
Use
.B h/[
and
.B l/]
to cycle pane focus,
.B j/k
to select with wrap-around,
.B PgUp/PgDn
and
.B Ctrl+U/D
to scroll,
.B Space
to freeze,
.B s
to cycle network scope,
.B c
and
.B v
to cycle context and role filters, and
.B a/A
and
.B m/u
to manage local incident review state. Mouse clicks switch tabs, select rows,
focus panes and choose the network scope. Use
.B ?
for help and
.B Esc
to close help without quitting.
.TP
.B doctor
Check systemd status, socket/group access, BTF, tracefs, probes, capture loss, storage headroom, configuration and noise.
.TP
.B status
Daemon health, attached probes, capture loss, storage state and effective configuration.
.TP
.B activity
Recent observed events.
.TP
.B apps
Applications and tasks with event and byte totals.
.TP
.BI app " NAME|ID"
Activity for one application, application ID or task ID.
.TP
.BI process " PID|ID"
Process metadata and exec history.
.TP
.BI tree " [PID|ID]"
Retained process descendants.
.TP
.BI file " PATH"
File activity for an exact path.
.TP
.BI why " PATH"
Processes that accessed or mutated a path, with evidence.
.TP
.B network
Recent network observations.
.TP
.B flows
TCP/UDP flow lifecycles, bytes, contributors, network context, role and exposure.
.TP
.B netns
List network namespaces and containers with apps, listeners, published ports, Docker/Podman port mappings, LXC DNAT fallback, vopono provider/protocol/server, forwarded-port renewal and health metadata, and byte totals.
.TP
.BI explain " network " APP
Combine flows, network context, roles and file activity into a semantic network verdict for an application.
.TP
.B summaries
Build, save, startup and download-like summaries.
.TP
.B incidents
Deterministic-rule incidents.
.TP
.B focus
Summarise configured focus rules, matching activity, flows, incidents and auto-detected harness logs.
.TP
.BI investigate " ID"
Render a complete Markdown investigation prompt and evidence bundle for an incident. Electric-eye does not call a model itself.

.TP
.B noise
Suggest likely capture filters, rule allowlists and noisy correlations. The suggestion is reviewable TOML; nothing is applied.
.TP
.B db status
Database size, WAL, table counts, retention window, disk headroom and storage drops.
.TP
.B db compact
Flush pending writes, VACUUM the database and truncate the WAL.
.TP
.B config show
Print the effective TOML configuration.
.TP
.BI config validate " PATH"
Validate a configuration file without starting the daemon.
.TP
.BI export " KIND"
Write JSONL for
.BR activity ", " incidents ", " flows ", " summaries ", " apps " or " noise .
.TP
.BI ack " INCIDENT-ID"
Locally acknowledge an incident; optional
.B \-\-for
sets an expiry.
.TP
.BI unack " INCIDENT-ID"
Remove a local acknowledgement.
.TP
.BI mute " APP RULE"
Locally mute matching incidents for one hour by default; optional
.B \-\-for
sets an expiry.
.TP
.BI unmute " APP RULE"
Remove a local mute.
.TP
.BI completions " SHELL"
Print a completion script for
.BR bash ", " zsh " or " fish .
.TP
.B mcp
Run the MCP stdio bridge to the daemon's MCP socket.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
electric-eye status
electric-eye doctor
electric-eye tui
electric-eye incidents --since 1h --severity high
electric-eye activity --follow
electric-eye export incidents --since 24h > incidents.jsonl
electric-eye db status
electric-eye noise
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ELECTRIC_EYE_SOCKET
Default query socket override.
.TP
.B ELECTRIC_EYE_MCP_SOCKET
Default MCP socket override.
.TP
.B ELECTRIC_EYED
Path to the daemon binary used by
.BR "config validate" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/electric-eye/electric-eye.sock
Query API socket.
.TP
.I /run/electric-eye/mcp.sock
MCP socket.
.TP
.I /etc/electric-eye/config.toml
System configuration fallback.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR electric-eyed (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
